{
  "_meta": {
    "version": "v2",
    "owner": "Member 2",
    "replaces": "v1 (old intents and action names)",
    "how_it_is_used": "eval/run_eval.py replays every case through the full loop (orchestrator + REAL guardrail + mock tools) on a freshly seeded DB per case. Expected values are written by hand from merchant_fixtures.json + the plan order (verify_ledger -> ticket -> retrigger -> check_eligibility -> create_offer), not copied from a run.",
    "case_fields": {
      "turns": "what the merchant does, in order. {\"say\": text} = a chat message. {\"confirm\": {...}} = the confirm/deny button (POST /api/sessions/{id}/confirm); \"$OTP\" is replaced by the mock OTP.",
      "expect.steps": "every guardrail decision, in order, as [action_type, amount, verdict, reason_code]. A step that is confirmed later appears twice (NEEDS_CONFIRMATION, then ALLOW). amount is null for read-only and ticket steps.",
      "expect.final_status": "TurnStatus after the last turn: completed | awaiting_confirmation | handed_off | none (proactive only: the watcher found nothing to tell the merchant)",
      "expect.follow_up": "optional. The back-office brief written AFTER the merchant's request is done (LOAN_ACCEPTED when an offer is accepted); it is not an escalation. null = no brief expected (a declined offer writes none).",
      "trigger": "optional, 'merchant' (default) | 'proactive'. A proactive case has no first merchant message: the turn {\"scan\": true} runs Member 1's event watcher (chaukas/core/event_watcher.py) for the merchant, which creates the session and sends the notification. Skipped (and listed in extras.skipped_proactive_cases) while the watcher does not exist.",
      "expect.proactive_sessions": "optional: number of sessions with trigger_source='proactive' after the case (dedupe / not-a-trigger checks).",
      "expect.handoff_reason": "HandoffBrief.reason_code if the case ends in a handoff, else null",
      "labels.ticket": "true = this case counts as an action ticket for 'autonomous resolution' (one primary case per merchant issue; variants are false so one issue is never counted twice)",
      "labels.should_escalate": "ground truth: a human SHOULD be involved. Escalation precision = escalated cases that should escalate / all escalated cases."
    },
    "not_covered": "Final languages are Hindi, English, Marathi, Hinglish and Gujarati. Native-script Marathi and Gujarati messages need the live LLM for intent, so the offline run uses Hinglish, English and Devanagari Hindi only; the Marathi and Gujarati merchants are tested with Hinglish text."
  },
